AcquisitionMethod: top 12 method
AlkylationReagent: iodoacetamide
CleavageAgent: MS-grade trypsin
CollisionEnergy: normalized fragmentation energy at 27%
Disease: house dust mite allergic individuals
EnrichmentMethod: peptides were enriched and desalted using 100 μl Pierce C18 Tips (Thermo Fisher Scientific)
FlowRateChromatogram: 300 nl/min
GradientTime: 5–45% B in 120 min
Instrument: Q Exactive Orbitrap mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific)
IonizationType: nano electrospray
Modification: carbamidomethylation (C)
Modification: deamidation (NQ)
Modification: oxidation (M)
NumberOfSamples: 16
NumberOfTechnicalReplicates: 4 to 6 independent experiments for each sample
Organism: Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus
Organism: Dermatophagoides farinae
Organism: Blomia tropicalis
Organism: Suidasia medanensis
Organism: Cicer arietinum
Organism: baker's yeast
PooledSample: pooled
ReductionReagent: dithiothreitol (DTT)
Separation: reverse-phase nano-HPLC (Dionex Ultimate 3000, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Bremen, Germany), directly coupled via nano electrospray to a Q Exactive Orbitrap mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific)
Separation: The column (Acclaim PepMap RSLC C18, 75 μm × 15 cm, Dionex, Thermo Fisher Scientific) was developed with an acetonitrile gradient
